IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `acc-types`
IMPORT `acc-s55`

-- Accident Compensation Act 2001 — GOALS 5 AND 6.
--
--   Goal 5: "When is a levy due, what refund or penalty follows, how is a
--            levy split across employers or mixed earnings, and what may an
--            earner buy in weekly compensation?"
--   Goal 6: "Is this an offence, what is the most it costs, when must the
--            charge be laid, and may the person sue for damages instead?"
--
-- Source: ../source/ACC2001.txt — Part 6 (ss 165-258), Part 9 (ss 294-336C),
-- Schedule 4.

§ `Goal 5 — levies and the Scheme`

-- ss 168(3), 168A(3), 168B(3), 250(2): a levy is due on the date specified,
-- "being a date not less than 30 days after the date of the invoice".
@ref ss 168(3), 168A(3), 168B(3), 250(2)
GIVEN invoiced IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the earliest due date for a levy invoiced on` invoiced MEANS invoiced PLUS 30

-- s 172(2)(b): where several employers paid levy on one employee's earnings
-- above the specified maximum, each may claim a refund of (a ÷ b) × c — a its
-- levied earnings, b all employers' levied earnings, c the total excess levy;
-- (3) not "after the expiry of a period of 4 years beginning from the close of
-- the tax year".
@ref s 172(2)(b)
GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER, `c` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the pro rata Work Account refund, a` `a` `, b` `b` `, c` `c` MEANS (`a` DIVIDED BY `b`) TIMES `c`

-- s 231(2)-(3): a person with both employee and self-employed earnings pays
-- earner levy on self-employed earnings only up to "the lesser of — (a) the
-- specified maximum ... reduced by the person's earnings as an employee ...;
-- and (b) the person's earnings as a self-employed person"; nothing if the
-- employee earnings already exceed the maximum.
@ref s 231(2)-(3)
GIVEN `specified maximum` IS A NUMBER, `employee earnings` IS A NUMBER, `self-employed earnings` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the self-employed earnings liable to earner levy, maximum` `specified maximum` `, employee earnings` `employee earnings` `, self-employed earnings` `self-employed earnings` MEANS
    IF `employee earnings` AT LEAST `specified maximum` THEN 0
    ELSE IF `specified maximum` MINUS `employee earnings` LESS THAN `self-employed earnings`
         THEN `specified maximum` MINUS `employee earnings`
         ELSE `self-employed earnings`

-- s 173(2): after estimating, refund an overpayment "greater than $20" (with
-- interest if it exceeds $1,000), or require an outstanding amount "greater
-- than $20". s 255(2): refunds under $20 may be withheld.
@ref s 173(2)-(3)
GIVEN `levy paid` IS A NUMBER, `levy actually payable` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the levy adjustment after estimate, paid` `levy paid` `, payable` `levy actually payable` MEANS
    IF `the difference` GREATER THAN 20 OR `the difference` LESS THAN (0 MINUS 20) THEN `the difference` ELSE 0
    WHERE
        `the difference` MEANS `levy actually payable` MINUS `levy paid`

-- s 174(2)(a): an employer who expects a change in relevant earnings "of 20%
-- or more" must notify its estimate.
@ref s 174(2)
GIVEN `last year` IS A NUMBER, `this year expected` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the employer must notify the changed earnings, last year` `last year` `, expected` `this year expected` IF
    (`this year expected` MINUS `last year`) TIMES 100 AT LEAST `last year` TIMES 20
    OR (`last year` MINUS `this year expected`) TIMES 100 AT LEAST `last year` TIMES 20

-- s 250(4)-(6): if unpaid levy, instalments and interest are not paid "within
-- 210 days after the due date", a further 10% penalty, and another 10% every
-- 180 days after; interest and penalties together never more than "3 times
-- the amount of the unpaid levy". (5): 15 days' notice first. Day 210 is
-- still "within 210 days", so the first penalty falls on day 211 and the
-- next on day 391.
@ref s 250(4), (6)
GIVEN `days after due` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the late levy penalty rounds, days after due` `days after due` MEANS
    IF `days after due` AT MOST 210 THEN 0
    ELSE 1 PLUS FLOOR ((`days after due` MINUS 211) DIVIDED BY 180)

@ref s 250(6)
GIVEN `unpaid levy` IS A NUMBER, `interest and penalties` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the interest and penalties payable, capped, on unpaid levy` `unpaid levy` `, accrued` `interest and penalties` MEANS
    IF `interest and penalties` GREATER THAN `unpaid levy` TIMES 3 THEN `unpaid levy` TIMES 3 ELSE `interest and penalties`

-- s 249(1): "(a) a penalty of 10% of an overpayment" for failing to tell the
-- Corporation what the person ought to have known was relevant; "(b) ... up to
-- 3 times the overpayment" for a knowingly incorrect statement.
@ref s 249(1)
GIVEN overpayment IS A NUMBER, `knowingly incorrect statement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the most overpayment penalty on` overpayment `, knowingly incorrect:` `knowingly incorrect statement` MEANS
    IF `knowingly incorrect statement` THEN overpayment TIMES 3 ELSE overpayment TIMES 10 DIVIDED BY 100

-- s 243(3): no new or altered levy determination "after the expiration of 4
-- years beginning on the close of the tax year in which the statement was
-- made", unless fraudulent or wilfully misleading. s 254(1): recovery of a
-- levy, penalty or interest "until the expiry of 10 years". s 255(3): no
-- refund of Commissioner-collected amounts after 8 years.
@ref s 243(3)
GIVEN `tax year ended` IS A DATE, `fraudulent or wilfully misleading` IS A BOOLEAN, `as at` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Corporation may still determine the levy, tax year ended` `tax year ended` `, fraudulent:` `fraudulent or wilfully misleading` `, as at` `as at` IF
    `fraudulent or wilfully misleading` OR `as at` AT MOST `add years` `tax year ended` 4

@ref s 254(1)
GIVEN payable IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`a levy may be recovered until, payable` payable MEANS `the last day under s 55 for a deadline of` (`add years` payable 10)

-- s 232(2): an employer ceasing business notifies "by the 15th day of the
-- second month after the month in which" it ceases.
@ref s 232(2)
GIVEN ceased IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`a ceasing employer must notify by, ceased` ceased MEANS `the last day under s 55 for a deadline of` (`add months` (Date 15 (DATE_MONTH ceased) (DATE_YEAR ceased)) 2)

-- s 181 "claim management period": "not less than 12 months and not more than
-- 60 months from the date of the injury".
@ref s 181 "claim management period"
GIVEN months IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an allowed claim management period in months of` months IF months AT LEAST 12 AND months AT MOST 60

-- s 209(2): purchased weekly compensation not less than 80% of the minimum
-- weekly earnings, nor more than the cl 46 maximum.
@ref s 209(2)
GIVEN `level sought` IS A NUMBER, `minimum weekly earnings` IS A NUMBER, maximum IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a purchasable level of weekly compensation, level` `level sought` `, minimum earnings` `minimum weekly earnings` `, maximum` maximum IF
    `level sought` TIMES 100 AT LEAST `minimum weekly earnings` TIMES 80 AND `level sought` AT MOST maximum

-- s 223(2)-(3): an earner may buy cover for periods out of work if applying
-- "while still in employment or within 1 month after ceasing employment",
-- for "not ... more than 2 years". s 224(2): payable "for not more than 5
-- years". s 226(2): an early termination refund only if more than 3 months
-- remain.
@ref s 223(2)(a), (3)(b)
GIVEN `ceased employment` IS A MAYBE DATE, applied IS A DATE, `years sought` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may buy weekly compensation, ceased` `ceased employment` `, applied` applied `, years sought` `years sought` IF
        `years sought` AT MOST 2
    AND CONSIDER `ceased employment`
        WHEN JUST c  THEN applied AT MOST `add months` c 1
        WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE

@ref s 226(2)
GIVEN `months remaining` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a refund follows early termination, months remaining` `months remaining` IF `months remaining` GREATER THAN 3

-- s 214(4)(b): absent regulations, the fuel levy is "5.08 cents per litre of
-- motor spirit".
@ref s 214(4)(b)
GIVEN litres IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the default fuel levy in dollars on litres` litres MEANS litres TIMES 5.08 DIVIDED BY 100

§ `Goal 6 — offences and proceedings`

-- The maximum for each offence. s 315: an offence with no stated fine — "a
-- fine not exceeding $500" (ss 98(3), 242). s 160(4): $1,000 (individual),
-- $5,000 (body corporate). s 308(4): "imprisonment for a term not exceeding 3
-- months or a fine not exceeding $5,000". s 309(5): $2,000. s 310(3):
-- $5,000. s 316(3): "imprisonment ... not exceeding 5 years or a fine not
-- exceeding $50,000"; (4): $25,000 first, $50,000 later. s 335: regulations
-- up to $500.
@ref ss 98(3), 160(4), 242, 308(4), 309(5), 310(3), 315, 316(3)-(4), 335
GIVEN o IS AN `ACC offence`
GIVETH AN `ACC penalty`
`the maximum penalty for` o MEANS
    CONSIDER o
    WHEN `s 98(3) an employer not paying first week compensation`           THEN `ACC penalty` OF 500,   0,  FALSE
    WHEN `s 160(4) breaching a non-publication order, individual`           THEN `ACC penalty` OF 1000,  0,  FALSE
    WHEN `s 160(4) breaching a non-publication order, body corporate`       THEN `ACC penalty` OF 5000,  0,  FALSE
    WHEN `s 242 intentionally not providing a statement of earnings`        THEN `ACC penalty` OF 500,   0,  FALSE
    WHEN `s 308 misleading the Corporation`                                 THEN `ACC penalty` OF 5000,  3,  TRUE
    WHEN `s 309 not providing requested information`                        THEN `ACC penalty` OF 2000,  0,  FALSE
    WHEN `s 310 not reporting increased earnings`                           THEN `ACC penalty` OF 5000,  0,  FALSE
    WHEN `s 316(1)(b) misapplying levy deductions`                          THEN `ACC penalty` OF 50000, 60, TRUE
    WHEN `s 316(1)(a), (c)-(e) a deduction offence, first conviction`       THEN `ACC penalty` OF 25000, 0,  FALSE
    WHEN `s 316(1)(a), (c)-(e) a deduction offence, later conviction`       THEN `ACC penalty` OF 50000, 0,  FALSE
    WHEN `an offence against regulations (s 335)`                           THEN `ACC penalty` OF 500,   0,  FALSE

-- s 309(4): the information offence applies only if "the claimant has
-- authorised the request" and the person has notice of it; (3) "without
-- reasonable excuse".
@ref s 309(3)-(4)
GIVEN `the claimant authorised the request, with notice` IS A BOOLEAN, `failed without reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the s 309 offence is committed, authorised:` `the claimant authorised the request, with notice` `, no excuse:` `failed without reasonable excuse` IF
    `the claimant authorised the request, with notice` AND `failed without reasonable excuse`

-- s 316(2): no conviction under (1)(a) if the deduction was paid and the late
-- payment was due to "illness, accident, or other cause beyond the person's
-- control".
@ref s 316(2)
GIVEN `the deduction was paid` IS A BOOLEAN, `late for a cause beyond control` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the s 316(1)(a) defence is made out, paid:` `the deduction was paid` `, beyond control:` `late for a cause beyond control` IF
    `the deduction was paid` AND `late for a cause beyond control`

-- s 313(1): the limitation period "ends on the date that is 5 years after the
-- termination of the year in which the offence was committed". FORK F6:
-- "year" is read as the calendar year.
@ref s 313(1)
GIVEN committed IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`a charge must be laid by, offence committed` committed MEANS `the last day under s 55 for a deadline of` (Date 31 12 (DATE_YEAR committed PLUS 5))

-- s 317(1): no proceedings "independently of this Act ... for damages arising
-- directly or indirectly out of personal injury covered by this Act"; (2)
-- except damage to property, an express contract term, or a personal
-- grievance (but no compensation for the injury itself, (3)); (4) Health and
-- Disability Commissioner and Human Rights Act proceedings; (5) carriage of
-- passengers conventions. s 319: exemplary damages remain available.
@ref ss 317, 319
GIVEN p IS A `Proceeding kind`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the proceeding may be brought despite cover,` p IF NOT p EQUALS `damages for the covered personal injury`

§§ `Provisions carried as text`

@ref ss 165-171, 172A, 175-180, 182-208, 210-213, 214(1)-(3), (4A)-(5), 215-230, 233-242, 244-248, 251-253, 255-258, 259-293, 294-307, 311, 312, 314, 318, 320-336C; Parts 10, 11; Schedules 1AA, 4-8
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`levy and general provisions carried as text` MEANS
    LIST "ss 165-171, 175-180: the Corporation's duty, the Accounts, Work Account levies, classification, risk adjustment and safety audits"
         "ss 181-191: accredited employers and shareholder-employee purchase"
         "ss 208-230: purchased weekly compensation by self-employed persons; the Motor Vehicle, Earners', Non-Earners' and Treatment Injury Accounts and their levies"
         "ss 233-248, 251-258: levies on ceasing, instalments, challenges, revision, determinations, statements, exempt amounts, the Commissioner as agent, information, debts, recovery limits, social security reimbursement, refunds, documents"
         "Parts 7, 8: the Corporation's constitution, functions, injury prevention, accountability, investments, reporting, information sharing, and the injury information manager"
         "ss 294-307: previous insurers, pre-2002 gradual process recovery, no contracting out, public health acute services, sick leave for non-work injury, how documents are given"
         "ss 311, 312, 318, 320-336C: GST on penalties, directors' liability, gradual process proceedings, the Corporation heard, its powers where proceedings exist, regulation-making powers"
         "Parts 10, 11 and Schedule 1AA: the 1998-2002 transition and pre-2002 cover and entitlements"
         "Schedules 4-8: levy deductions, the Corporation's board and staff, and consequential matters"
